content.text:
The `shouldCondenseWithOverlapCheck` code at lines 728-734 has a read-only session gate:

```go
if isActive && isRecentInteraction(lastInteraction) {
    if h.sessionsWithCommittedFiles > 0 && len(h.filesTouchedBefore) == 0 {
        // skipping read-only ACTIVE session
        return false
    }
    return true
}
```

And for IDLE sessions with no files touched (line 737-738):
```go
if len(h.filesTouchedBefore) == 0 {
    return false // No files tracked = no overlap evidence
}
```

So there ARE guards against condensing read-only sessions... but this Codex session *was* condensed (metadata exists). Let me check when these guards were added:

